Actually, that's exactly the direction I think you should take the project.

What you're describing is not just detection. It's called Autonomous Incident Response or Self-Healing Cyber Defense.

So instead of this:

Detect Attack

↓

Alert User

↓

Wait for Human

your ACTDRS would do this:

Monitor

↓

Detect

↓

Analyze

↓

Decide

↓

Take Action

↓

Verify

↓

Notify Owner

This is much more powerful.

Example 1 – SSH Brute Force Attack

Suppose a hacker tries to guess your password.

Current security software
Attack detected

↓

Notification

↓

You manually block the IP
Your ACTDRS
Attack detected

↓

AI analyzes

↓

"Brute-force attack"

↓

Block attacker's IP

↓

Verify attack stopped

↓

Generate report

↓

Send notification

Notification:

⚠️ Brute-force attack detected from IP 185.xxx.xxx.xxx.

I blocked the attacker's IP using the firewall.

SSH service is operating normally.

Your system is currently protected.

Notice that the action has already been taken before the notification is sent.

